# cppcheck suppressions — SomnoTrace
#
# Every entry names ONE finding, why it is a false positive, and is anchored to a
# FILE AND LINE on purpose. A line-anchored suppression stops matching when the code
# moves, which turns the gate red and asks a human to look again — the opposite of a
# file-wide suppression, which would silently hide a real future finding of the same
# kind in the same file. Loud drift beats quiet coverage loss.
#
# Verified against cppcheck 2.19.0 on main @ 1ac2d48 (2026-09-06).

# The ESP-IDF EMBED_FILES idiom. `PORTAL_HTML_LEN` is
# `(_binary_portal_html_end - _binary_portal_html_start)` (net_provision.c:676-677) —
# two linker symbols that bound one embedded blob. cppcheck sees two unrelated extern
# objects being subtracted and cannot know the linker placed them at the ends of the
# same region. Removing the idiom is not an option: it is how ESP-IDF exposes an
# embedded file's length.
subtractPointers:main/net_provision.c:732

# Interprocedural initialisation through an out-parameter. `bes` is a local array of
# pointers filled by `uploader_enabled_backends(bes, UPLOAD_MAX_BACKENDS)`, which writes
# `out[n++] = s_backends[i]` and RETURNS the count; the loop below reads only `bes[i]`
# for `i < n`. cppcheck does not follow the callee's writes through the pointer
# parameter, and the message gives it away — it lists struct FIELDS (`bes.id`,
# `bes.label`), so it has lost the array-of-pointers type entirely.
uninitvar:components/uploader/upload_sched.c:601
